{
  "_comment": "Valmera render box 2 (h2): the owner factory's home. Contabo Cloud VPS 16: 16 shared vCPU / 64 GB / 250 GB NVMe, US West. Same contract as box.json (box 1): each slot's --cpus is a ceiling for ONE job, slots oversubscribe the CPU on purpose and per-call cgroup CPU weights (customers 4x the owner factory) divide it under contention; memory limits are the measured p95 with headroom. As the factory's home the owner caps are high (interactive 10 of 12, batch 5 of 6, mcp 14 of 16, agent 4, shorts 3), which still leaves customers who overflow here a slot in every lane; customers always rank first in the queue. Parity: interactive slots see 2 CPUs and batch slots 4 (cpusets), exactly Cloudflare's standard-3/standard-4 lanes and box 1, so renders are bit-identical across boxes. Selected on this host by /etc/valmera/plan (box/host/add_box.sh).",
